From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Drop the embedded prebuilt JDT LS jars

Upstream embeds three prebuilt jars with include_bytes!: the Java usages
and Kotlin bridge JDT LS extensions, which only build against the Eclipse
JDT LS jars, and a patched Lombok agent. They are removed from the source
archive. Without the extensions Find Usages falls back to standard LSP
references and Kotlin libraries are not bridged into the Java model, as
upstream already does when they fail to install. The Lombok tool entry
goes back to its 0.1.30 form; jdtls takes Lombok from the project's
Maven or Gradle cache or a -javaagent option. The tests of the embedded
jars go with them.

--- a/crates/ide-sdk/src/java.rs
+++ b/crates/ide-sdk/src/java.rs
@@ -1153,137 +1155,16 @@
 
